diff --git a/docs/design/acrobat-archer.md b/docs/design/acrobat-archer.md
index 2e63d7b..2f7c1f0 100644
--- a/docs/design/acrobat-archer.md
+++ b/docs/design/acrobat-archer.md
@@ -71,3 +71,9 @@ Acrobat Archer).
   px; Firework Arrow ~58 px round (its blast is 50-80; it was ~20); Grand Somersault's ring ~95 px
   round (was ~31), and her rain now lands as a gold ring racing out to its 210 px edge
   (`celshockmint`); the springboard is half again as big.
+
+## Her skills in her paths (2026-11-04)
+
+Her paths keep Handspring, Springboard and Grand Somersault but play them their own way
+(`src/data/path-skills.js`): the Phantom Trickster's Vanishing Act, Top Hat and Levitation, the
+Arbalist Engineer's Steam Hop, Spring Mine and Bolt Mortar (see their design docs). Hers are unchanged.
diff --git a/docs/design/arbalist.md b/docs/design/arbalist.md
index 20f8b12..230e26e 100644
--- a/docs/design/arbalist.md
+++ b/docs/design/arbalist.md
@@ -78,3 +78,20 @@ Kestrel's trial carry over; the name is Arbalist Engineer).
   px long and ~70 tall (its hit band is 140); the hit mark ~40-58 px; Sticky Bolt's blast ~66 px
   round (its reach is 50-80; it was ~26); Steam Vent's steam ~60 px round for its 80 px reach (was
   ~13). Muzzle and leap puffs keep their size.
+
+## Her own Acrobat skills (2026-11-04)
+
+The Acrobat Archer's skills she keeps (same numbers) are now her own gadgets (`src/data/path-skills.js`):
+
+- **Handspring is Steam Hop** (`aejet`): she crouches and slaps the valve on her belt, her boots blast
+  steam and she rockets over the monster in a tucked arc with the crossbow hugged low and her free
+  arm windmilling; lands in a skid with another burst of steam, spins round on her heel and fires back.
+- **Grand Somersault is Bolt Mortar** (`aemortar`): down on one knee she stands the crossbow on its
+  stock at arm's length, nose to the sky, cranks it three times, and fires a brass shell straight up
+  with a kick that rocks her back; it bursts high overhead (`celaeshell`: a brass flash, a teal ring,
+  cogs and steam) and a hail of her teal bolts rains down on everything below while she watches with
+  her head tipped back, bounces up pumping her fist, and gives a thumbs up.
+- **Springboard is Spring Mine** (`aewind`): a wide squat, the brass plate dropped in front of her,
+  its key wound round twice with her whole body swinging into it, a test poke, and two hops back
+  pointing at it. The mine (`celaemine`) blinks teal with its key turning, and goes off in a jump of
+  its lid, cogs and steam.
diff --git a/docs/design/making-a-job.md b/docs/design/making-a-job.md
index 9250599..48b3ec2 100644
--- a/docs/design/making-a-job.md
+++ b/docs/design/making-a-job.md
@@ -59,6 +59,12 @@ blow).
   (each set with its own finisher and mastery, gated by `weapons`), so the player chooses where
   the points go, and its own basic combo and command moves for each weapon.
 
+- **A second job plays its first job's skills its own way.** Same skill, key and numbers, but its
+  own move and effects, in its own colour and shapes (`paths` in the skill's `at()`, keyed by job id,
+  with `pathNames` for its name; the mechanism is `src/data/path-skills.js`). A new path isn't done
+  until every skill it can cast plays its own move (`tests/melee.test.js`, "no second job plays
+  another job's move").
+
 - **Check names before using them on the world.** The world already keeps the player's key
   presses as `intent`, so a gauge can't be called that.
 
diff --git a/docs/design/phantom-trickster.md b/docs/design/phantom-trickster.md
index b9da093..e644c42 100644
--- a/docs/design/phantom-trickster.md
+++ b/docs/design/phantom-trickster.md
@@ -74,3 +74,21 @@ Built, replacing the Beastmaster in place (the path keeps the `beastmaster` id a
   ~22 px; the hit mark ~36-50 px. Smoke Bomb's smoke is ~120 px wide (was ~30 for a 100-140 px
   reach) and a plum ring of smoke and cards rolls out to the reach (`celshockplum`). Trick puffs
   and Grand Illusion's smoke are larger too.
+
+## Her own Acrobat skills (2026-11-04)
+
+The Acrobat Archer's skills she keeps (same numbers) are now her own tricks (`src/data/path-skills.js`):
+
+- **Handspring is Vanishing Act** (`ptvanish`): a flick of the hand and a cape sweep with a half turn
+  and a wink, and she is gone in a puff of plum smoke (actually unseen, `world.vanish`); she steps out
+  of another puff behind the monster already turning, draws as she comes round and looses back.
+- **Grand Somersault is Levitation** (`ptlevitate`): the magician's levitation. A whirl of the cape,
+  then she floats up and lies back flat on the air, toes pointed; at the top she swings upright and
+  snaps her fingers, a giant top hat (`celpthat`) appears over the stage, flips over and pours plum
+  arrows, cards and doves down on everything below while she looses up into it (the rain falls as
+  her plum arrows); she drifts down into a deep stage bow.
+- **Springboard is Top Hat** (`pthattrap`): she tips her hat, sweeps it off in a bow, sets it down
+  brim-up and taps it twice with her bow; it rocks with a twinkle until a monster steps in, then hops
+  and doves and cards burst out of it as it flings them up (`celpttrap`).
+- Firework Arrow already bursts in her smoke, and the trap's spring and the buff power-up come in her
+  plum now too.
diff --git a/docs/design/warrior-line.md b/docs/design/warrior-line.md
index 9852db0..a0c77fd 100644
--- a/docs/design/warrior-line.md
+++ b/docs/design/warrior-line.md
@@ -34,3 +34,31 @@ Effects, measured against the hits' reach:
 - The Paladin's shield flare on a bash is a fifth bigger.
 - The big rings (Titan Breaker, Grand Verdict, Crimson Eclipse, Hallowed Ground, Rampage) already
   ran out to their reach and were left as they were.
+
+## Each path's own Warrior skills (2026-11-04)
+
+The Warrior's skills stay with the paths (same key, numbers and purpose), but each path now plays
+them its own way (the player's pick, "own version per path"). The mechanism is generic and lives in
+`src/data/path-skills.js`: a skill's `at()` returns `paths` keyed by job id (a combo array, or an
+object laid over its params), and `pathNames` gives its name per path in the skills window.
+
+- **Shoulder Charge:** Shield Rush (Paladin) and Reckless Charge (Berserker), as before.
+- **Titan Breaker:** the Paladin's **Heaven's Seal** (`plseal`): no leap; a knight's rite. She raises
+  the blade upright in a salute and rises on her toes, eyes closed, while a great gold crest of light
+  (`celplcrest`, a kite shield with her cross and gold star in a halo) gathers over her; one planted
+  two-handed chop with a stamp brings the crest down onto them (a cross of light, gold rock, a ring
+  out to the reach); she swoops the blade back up to the sky and pillars of light burst up in a ring
+  out to the aftershock's reach, then holds it out low and level. The Berserker's **Skyfall Rend**
+  (`bkpounce`): a beast's crouch and a howl as fire flares under him, a long pounce with the axe flung
+  back and limbs spread, then he falls head-first in a meteor of rose fire (`celbkmeteor`, carried
+  with him, under him) and smashes down; claw gashes tear the ground and a jagged ring rips out; he
+  wrenches the axe up out of the earth in a burst of fire and roars.
+- **Whirlwind** (the proc after a combo's last swing; `WHIRLS` in world/melee.js): the Paladin's
+  **Halo Rotor** (`plrotor`): the blade swept round flat over her head like a rotor while she marches
+  under it, gold arcs overhead, ending in a forward shield-shove that flares her light shield and
